\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Admissible protocol class}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{post-training}

\p{For a fixed base artifact #{M_0}, an \strong{admissible protocol class}
#{\mathfrak P(M_0)} is a declared set of post-training procedures that start
from #{M_0} and may be compared in one potential calculation. Membership
fixes the allowed data access, feedback sources, environment
interfaces, update families, stopping rules, and randomization.}

\p{This is an FTIP proposal. Restricting the class is mathematically necessary:
an unrestricted procedure could import a test answer, call an undeclared
teacher, or spend unbounded external computation.}

\p{A theorem about #{\mathfrak P(M_0)} must state which fields are fixed and which
are optimized. Results for reward-only reweighting, active environment
interaction, and external demonstrations belong to different classes unless a
larger class names all three.}
